---
title: "Radiographic Pathology"
code: "RAD-240"
category: "radiography"
credits: "3"
prerequisites: []
corequisites: []
prerequisiteNote: "Prerequisite: BIO 141-142 and RAD 121-221"
---

Presents a survey of common medical and surgical disorders that affect radiographic image. Discusses conditions related to different systems of the human body. Studies the correlation of these conditions with radiographs. Lecture 3 hours per week. Additional course fee applies.
